  "articleBody": "When hail hits Alvarado, it can leave homeowners in a tough spot: do you need a roof repair, or is a full replacement necessary? It’s a common question, and getting the right answer can save you a lot of stress and money. Hail damage isn't always obvious, and what looks minor from the ground could be more extensive. Making the best decision means understanding the extent of the damage and your roof's overall condition.\n\n### How to Compare Your Options\nComparing repair versus replacement largely depends on the severity and widespread nature of the hail damage, as well as your roof's age and existing condition. For localized damage, like a few missing shingles or minor dents, repairs can often be a cost-effective solution. Discounted Roofing Co. specializes in lasting repairs that keep your roof strong and protected. We use high-quality materials and provide a warranty on all our repair work, ensuring it holds up against future Texas weather.\n\nHowever, if the hail damage is extensive, affecting large sections of your roof, or if your roof is already older and nearing the end of its lifespan, a full replacement might be the more economical and protective long-term choice. Our team will conduct a free inspection to evaluate your roof thoroughly. We'll show you exactly what we see, providing clear documentation with photos and explanations. If a replacement is needed, we'll guide you through choosing the best roofing material for your home, budget, and our demanding Texas climate, including durable metal roofing options. We believe in honest recommendations – if repairs are enough, we’ll tell you. If a replacement is the better long-term solution, we’ll explain why, focusing on quality workmanship and fair pricing, with no games or surprises. This transparency helps you make a confident decision about one of your property’s most important protective systems.\n\nUnsure if your roof needs repair or replacement after hail? Contact Discounted Roofing Co. for an honest assessment and clear recommendations.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}